#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110813 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "7fe1fb12-e10b-5870-8007-02f1eb2f68f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $(xy^{2})^{2} \\cdot xy$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110915 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a9eb6cb-b287-518f-b5b6-3a57acbb1da3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186108275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\frac{100x^{7}y^{3}}{20x^{3}y^{2}}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111086 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d7c1ad1-12d2-56a0-a936-eae89426f942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1061 3561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ff971efe-57b1-5d6a-a9d6-53728830ae56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111594 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1061 3562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a787c3de-89d7-50ac-b1ff-50a2fb31a2ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111595 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1061 3565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8884d25c-0665-5e4b-b13b-866ef3ec66f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111596 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111597 #edb/ref 1061 3569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111597 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "73248b69-f18a-503e-b712-b3f56ae6841a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111597 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1061 37772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d8d59c7e-2b45-5493-a09c-f4211a690c16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111601 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes, we might need to use more than one rule of exponents to simplify an expression. First, let's remind ourselves of all of the rules of exponents.\n\n- Radicals as fractional exponents: $\\sqrt[n]{x} = x^{1/n}$\n- The product rule: $a^n \\cdot a^m = a^{n+m}$\n- The quotient rule: $\\dfrac{a^n}{a^m} = a^{n-m}$\n- The power rule: $\\left(a^m \\right)^n = a^{mn}$\n- The power of product rule: $(ab)^n = a^nb^n$\n- The power of quotient rule: $\\left(\\dfrac a b \\right)^n = \\dfrac{a^n}{b^n}$\n\nAs an example, let's simplify the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\left(u^2 v\\right)^3\n$$\n\nWe start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n(u^{2}v)^{3} = (u^{2})^{3} \\cdot v^{3}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(u^{2})^{3} \\cdot v^{3} &=  \\\\\nu^{(2 \\cdot 3)} \\cdot v^{3} &=  \\\\\nu^{6} \\cdot v^{3} &=  \\\\\n&= u^{6}v^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1065 1485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "13b1c64a-c868-5824-919e-c3a665bb4a96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111824 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111904 #edb/ref 1064 "To simplify the expression $x\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{x^2}$, we first rewrite the radical as a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\nx \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{x^2} = x \\cdot \\left(x^2 \\right)^{1/3}\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the power rule for exponents:\n\n$$\nx \\cdot \\left(x^2 \\right)^{1/3} = x \\cdot x^{2(1/3)} = x \\cdot x^{2/3}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx \\cdot x^{2/3} &=  \\\\\nx^{1 + 2/3} &=  \\\\\n&= x^{5/3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we express the result as a radical:\n\n$$\nx^{5/3} = \\sqrt[3]{x^5}\n$$\n\nNotice that, by combining the radicals as fractional exponents and power rules, we get the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[n]{x^m} = x^{m/n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111904 #edb/ref 1065 6221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111904 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "91debf57-af23-518b-b432-ea04beccc17a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111904 #edb/ref 1067 "Rules of Exponents and Radicals" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
